// The name-domain counterpart of `caps_elide_full_grant`: the grant on the
// `impl "std/env"` line is the domain's whole-resource `*`, so the runtime
// name check at `std/env`'s own forwarding calls (`has` over `has_raw`, and
// the three beside it) is provably going to pass and `cap_plan` drops it. The
// entry module's own check at the call site below stays: it is the one that
// still refuses a name with a `/` in it, since `*` crosses no `/`.
impl "std/env" caps(env = ["*"])

fun main() {
    print(env.has(name = "PATH") || true)
}
